---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/urls";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Equator"
  description="Equator is a small Czech family company making titanium bicycles and carbon wheels. Equator Scandinavia brings them to riders in the Nordics."
  image="images/sensei-2.jpg"
>
  <section class="wrap about-hero">
    <h1>A small company from Zlín.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Titanium bicycles and carbon wheels, made by people who plan for you to
      keep them a long time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure class="wrap about-photo">
    <Photo
      src="images/sensei-2.jpg"
      alt="Equator Sensei Gen 4 titanium bicycle on a gravel track between fields"
      sizes="100vw"
      eager
    />
  </figure>

  <article class="wrap story">
    <p>
      Equator Cycling is a small family company in Zlín, in the east of the
      Czech Republic. It believes cycling, like business, is about
      relationships, and it keeps both personal.
    </p>
    <p>
      It started with carbon wheels. Titanium frames followed as the logical
      next step. Every frame goes through several prototypes before it is
      released, and every bike is designed, tested and assembled in Czechia
      with parts from specialist suppliers around the world. The wheels are
      built and tested by hand in Equator's own workshop.
    </p>
    <p id="titanium">
      Titanium was chosen because it lasts. It doesn't rust, so the frames
      need no paint: just a brushed finish that wears its miles quietly. How a
      bike rides still comes down to its geometry and build, which is why each
      model has one clear purpose. Sensei for road and gravel, Raiden for the
      road, Yasei for the long way round.
    </p>
    <p>
      The range is small on purpose, and the conversation is direct. You talk
      to people who know the bikes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Equator Scandinavia brings these bikes and wheels to riders and shops in
      Denmark, Sweden and Norway, starting in Copenhagen. Tell us what you
      want to ride and we'll help you choose the right build. Every request is
      answered personally, and we confirm price, availability and delivery
      with Equator before anything is paid.
    </p>
    <div class="about-actions">
      <a class="button" href={url("bikes/")}>Explore the bikes</a>
      <a class="text-link" href={url("contact/")}>Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding: 72px 0 40px;
  }
  .about-hero .lead {
    max-width: 560px;
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-photo {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .about-photo :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 760px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .story {
    padding: 72px 0 112px;
  }
  .story > p {
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .story p {
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.3em;
    color: #444;
  }
  .story p:first-child {
    color: #171717;
  }
  .about-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .about-hero {
      padding: 44px 0 28px;
    }
    .story {
      padding: 44px 0 72px;
    }
    .story p {
      font-size: var(--fs-body);
    }
  }
</style>
